// Baggage & Policy constants based on airline public rules:
// - Southwest: Basic ($73 on sale / $111 reg): 1 personal item + 1 carry-on free + 2 checked bags free (or 1st checked bag promo/policy), seat assigned at check-in. Choice ($109 on sale): standard seat included in advance.
// - American Airlines: Main Cabin ($119): 1 personal item + 1 carry-on free, 1st checked bag $35-$40, standard seat selection included in advance, ticket changes permitted without change fee.
// - Delta Air Lines: Basic Economy ($120): 1 personal item + 1 carry-on free, 1st checked bag $35, seat assigned after check-in, no ticket changes. Main Cabin: seat selection included.
// - United Airlines: Basic Economy ($73-$93): 1 personal item ONLY (NO full-size carry-on permitted in overhead bin!), 1st checked bag $40 (or gate check fee $25 + $35 bag fee), seat assigned at check-in. Regular Economy: full carry-on included + standard seat selection (typically +$35-$40/person).
// - JetBlue: Blue Basic ($162-$163): 1 personal item + 1 carry-on free (JetBlue updated policy allows free carry-on across all fare types), 1st checked bag $35-$40, seat selection for a fee until check-in.
// - Frontier: Basic ($38-$117 teaser): 1 small personal item ONLY. Carry-on bag is $55-$65+ per bag each way! Checked bag is $50-$60+ each way. Seat assignment is $15-$30+ per person. For 3 adults, baggage + seats easily add $200-$250+, making the practical price much higher than the teaser fare.

